# Forma UI rules

- Use CSS variables from the design system (`--color-accent`, `--color-bg`, etc.); do not invent one-off brand colors.
- Public form fields: visible `<label>`, errors via `aria-describedby`, `aria-invalid` when wrong, required via `aria-required` or equivalent.
- Prefer native inputs/selects; custom controls need full keyboard support.
- Tap targets ≥ 44px on mobile for primary actions.
- Cards only when wrapping an interactive unit (e.g. question editor). Avoid decorative card grids on dashboards.
- Motion: only autosave feedback, question add/remove, submit→success — keep under ~200ms, no decorative animation noise.
- Dashboard = list/table first; builder = centered form canvas; public form = single column.
